<title>HONG KONG: Triplenic interim net rises 80 percent.</title>
<headline>Triplenic interim net rises 80 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   5.8	  vs 3.2 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	  vs 1.0 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  16.32 gain vs 4.68 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    21.41	vs 11.88</p>
<p>    Turnover		     40.86	vs 8.76</p>
<p>    Company name		 Triplenic Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Triplenic, formerly Kai Ming Investment Co Ltd, is a property investment and development company.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on disposals of the group's investment properties.</p>
<p>The company subdivided each ordinary share into eight new ordinary shares on July 31, 1996. Comparative share earnings and interim dividend have been adjusted accordingly.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
